{"groups":[{"members":["c1","c2"],"primary":"c2","title":"Santa Ana Rent Stabilization and Just Cause Eviction Ordinance: just cause eviction and relocation assistance","requirement":"After 30 days of tenancy, an owner may not terminate a tenancy without just cause stated in a written notice, such as non-payment of rent, breach of a material lease term, nuisance, criminal activity, owner move-in, withdrawal from the rental market, or demolition or substantial remodel, and must first give the tenant notice of a curable violation and time to cure it. For no-fault terminations, the owner must provide 3 months of relocation assistance or waive rent for the final 3 months of the tenancy.","key_value":"Just cause required after 30 days of tenancy; no-fault termination requires 3 months of relocation assistance or 3 months of waived rent","status":"in_force","effective_date":"2021-11-19","end_date":null,"citation":"Santa Ana Rent Stabilization and Just Cause Eviction Ordinance (adopted 2021)","coverage_conditions":"Residential rental property in Santa Ana, other than exempt property. Owners must notify existing tenants of the protections before December 19, 2021, or at lease commencement or renewal.","exemptions":"Housing produced in the last 15 years; deed-restricted affordable housing; hotel and transient occupancy; hospital and care facilities; dormitories; and other shared living quarters.","conflict_note":null}],"dropped":[]}
